# Architecture Documentation Rules

## Core Principles
1. Documentation Requirements
   - Architecture decisions must be documented
   - System patterns must be clear
   - Technical decisions need rationale
   - Performance metrics must be tracked

2. Required Files [CRITICAL]
   Must maintain:
   - systemPatterns.md
   - techContext.md
   - architecture/
     ├── diagrams/       # System visualizations
     ├── decisions/      # Technical decisions
     ├── patterns/       # Design patterns
     └── metrics/        # Performance data

3. Documentation Process
   - Document all decisions
   - Include alternatives considered
   - Track performance impact
   - Maintain diagrams
   - Record dependencies

## Documentation Standards
1. Required Sections
   systemPatterns.md:
   - Architecture Overview
   - Technical Decisions
   - Design Patterns
   - Integration Patterns
   - Error Handling
   - Best Practices
   - System Constraints
   - Implementation Metrics
   - Performance Metrics
   - Quality Metrics

   techContext.md:
   - Technology Stack
   - Dependencies
   - Infrastructure
   - Security
   - Performance
   - Scalability
   - Monitoring

2. File Structure
   Each file MUST have:
   - Version header
   - Last update timestamp
   - Table of contents
   - Clear hierarchy
   - Cross-references
   - Change log
   - Metrics section
   - Status indicators

## Workflows
1. Architecture Updates
   - Document decisions
   - Update diagrams
   - Record impacts
   - Track metrics
   - Update dependencies

2. Performance Tracking
   - Record metrics
   - Track trends
   - Note bottlenecks
   - Document solutions
   - Monitor improvements

3. Status Tracking
   Implementation Status:
   - ✅ Implemented
   - ⚠️ In Progress
   - ❌ Not Started
   - 🔄 Under Review
   - 🎯 Planned

   Priority Levels:
   - 🔥 Critical
   - 🚀 High
   - 📈 Medium
   - 📋 Low
   - 💡 Nice to Have

## Memory Commands
1. #load
   - Read architecture context
   - Check system patterns
   - Review metrics

2. #status
   - Save architecture state
   - Update diagrams
   - Record decisions
   - Update metrics

3. #next
   - Complete current task
   - Find next priority
   - Start fresh chat

## Metrics Requirements
1. Performance Metrics
   Must track:
   - Response times
   - Resource usage
   - Scalability limits
   - Bottlenecks
   - Optimization targets

2. Quality Metrics
   Must include:
   - Code coverage
   - Technical debt
   - Security score
   - Performance score
   - Maintainability index

3. Progress Metrics
   Must track:
   - Implementation status
   - Completion rates
   - Risk levels
   - Resource allocation
   - Dependencies